  "answer": "The conditions required for Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) include:\n\n1. **Target Client Software**: The target must be a client that allows scripting communication from remote hosts, such as a JavaScript-enabled web browser [Source 1].\n\n2. **Deployment of Hostile Service**: There must be an ability to deploy a custom hostile service that can be accessed by the targeted clients [Source 1].\n\n3. **Communication Capability**: The attacker must be able to communicate synchronously or asynchronously with the client machine [Source 1].\n\n4. **Required Skills**: High-level skills are needed to exploit a client-side vulnerability to inject malicious scripts into the browser's executable process. Lower-level skills may suffice for simpler attacks, such as placing scripts in user-generated content sites that are echoed back to other client machines [Source 2].",
